# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Farroway Frontend — Environment Variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env for local development, or set at build
# time for deployment. The launch gate verifies these
# are present before a production build.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — production build will not produce a working
# bundle without this. Web builds in dev fall back to
# '/api' (proxied by Vite) so leaving this blank is safe
# locally; CI/CD must set it for `vite build --mode
# production`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical name (May 2026 URL hardening spec §3).
# `VITE_API_URL` is accepted as a back-compat alias.
VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://your-api-server.com/api"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — only needed for Capacitor native builds
# or custom deployments where the API lives on a
# different origin from the static bundle.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-server.com/api

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Sentry error tracking
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, both client and server initialise their respective
# Sentry SDKs. The full pipeline:
#   • Client: @sentry/react in src/lib/sentry.js — captures
#     render-time crashes via the inner SystemErrorBoundary +
#     the global ErrorBoundary; auto-instruments routing /
#     navigation / fetch via browserTracingIntegration. Photo
#     dataURLs, blob: URLs, JWT tokens, Authorization headers,
#     cookies, and request bodies are stripped in beforeSend +
#     beforeBreadcrumb before the event leaves the browser.
#   • Server: @sentry/node in server/src/lib/sentry.js — the
#     existing errorHandler middleware captures every 5xx
#     server fault with request context (method/path/userId/
#     requestId), strips Authorization headers + cookies +
#     bodies in beforeSend, and skips ECONNRESET/aborted-
#     request noise.
#   • User tagging: AuthContext mirrors the signed-in user into
#     Sentry's session tag — id + role + country code only.
#     No email, phone, name, address.
# Both SDKs are no-ops when this is unset, matching the
# productionRuntime "Sentry disabled safely" banner. The
# server alias SENTRY_DSN is accepted under the same "sentry"
# service in the banner.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=""
#
# Dev-mode Sentry is OFF by default so personal browsers don't
# spam the prod project during local hacking. To opt in for a
# specific debugging session:
# VITE_SENTRY_ENABLE_DEV="1"
#
# Session Replay is OFF by default. Enable only after a privacy
# / consent review (replay records DOM structure + click timing
# even with maskAllText + blockAllMedia):
# VITE_SENTRY_REPLAY="1"

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production deployment notes
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Set VITE_API_BASE_URL in your hosting environment
#    (Railway → Variables, Vercel → Environment Variables,
#    Netlify → Site Settings → Environment).
# 2. Run `npm run launch-gate` locally with the same
#    value to confirm the build assertion passes.
# 3. The frontend never reads server-side secrets —
#    JWT, Twilio, SendGrid, etc. all live in the
#    server/.env file (see server/.env.example).
